{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death","id":831132,"title":"Dramatic Death Scene - How would a Sidereal fake their own death?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-16T10:30:40-08:00","id":831132,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Dramatic Death Scene - How would a Sidereal fake their own death?","content":"How would a Sidereal fake their own death? Ideally they would leave a corpse behind so there is no question that the Sidereal's Resplendent Destiny is dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T10:53:02-08:00","id":831138,"title":"","content":"Aside from that Sidereal Charm that lets you fake your own death? (Or was it a college ability, I don't recall)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T10:56:18-08:00","id":831142,"title":"","content":"There is a Sidereal Charm/College that lets you fake your own death!? What Ability?<br /> <br /> I know there is a resurrection charm in the Quicksilver Hand SMA, but you die Obi-Wan style, which leaves no corpse and is obviously supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-16-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:00:35-08:00","id":831146,"title":"","content":"I REALLY wish I remembered. I feel like there was a comic about it in one of the books. I don't have access to my 2nd ed stuff here at work so I can't look it up, but it basically told the whole world that you were dead until you gave them reason to suspect otherwise. Maybe I'm misremembering. I guess that's worse than unhelpful, teasing and not following through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:13:55-08:00","id":831158,"title":"","content":"I do have a copy of Ex3 at work. Apparently there is a Solar Craft Charm called Dual Magnus Prana (pg. 292) that lets you retroactively fake your death, if needed. I wonder if a Solar can build a simulacrum of someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:23:40-08:00","id":831164,"title":"","content":"Ceasing to exist approach doesn't leave a body, I suppose clever use of name pilfering practice could trick someone into thinking you died if all they knew you by was the stolen name. Ebon shadow style lets you supernaturally play dead but that requires the corpse eventually disappearing because that's your body. If none of those charms fit your fancy there's always custom sorcery spells, if anyone has the time or funding to make spells it's Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:30:59-08:00","id":831169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831158#post831158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a copy of Ex3 at work. Apparently there is a Solar Craft Charm called Dual Magnus Prana (pg. 292) that lets you retroactively fake your death, if needed. I wonder if a Solar can build a simulacrum of someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some INTENSE feelings about this charm on the forums, so be wary opening that can of worms. I wouldn't personally look at it as anything beyond the exact text of the charm. Saves YOU from death with cool flavor, and that's fuckin it. My 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:36:45-08:00","id":831173,"title":"","content":"A big explosion and a disposable body double?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:38:38-08:00","id":831176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831169#post831169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are some INTENSE feelings about this charm on the forums, so be wary opening that can of worms. I wouldn't personally look at it as anything beyond the exact text of the charm. Saves YOU from death with cool flavor, and that's fuckin it. My 2 cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Closes can of worms and slowly backs away*<br /> <br /> Basically, I wanted a Sidereal's Resplendent Destiny to become a Martyr for a cause. Doesn't seem to be a way to do this since all of the Sidereal charms makes the Sidereal cease to exist. It's kind of hard to be a Martyr if no one remembers you (I was going to get around this by having the duration of the RD extend past the identity's &quot;death&quot; for a while. )<br /> <br /> I guess I'll have to embrace Sidickery and have someone else become the Martyr of the cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:52:20-08:00","id":831188,"title":"","content":"I think for a sidereal, instead of being a martyr for a cause, convincing someone else into being a martyr for the same cause fits their theme better. They are usually behind the scenes guys, not the spotlight grabbing types.<br /> <br /> They can of course can use a martial art , sorcery or an artifact for the effect of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:06:48-08:00","id":831201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831188#post831188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for a sidereal, instead of being a martyr for a cause, convincing someone else into being a martyr for the same cause fits their theme better. They are usually behind the scenes guys, not the spotlight grabbing types.<br /> <br /> They can of course can use a martial art , sorcery or an artifact for the effect of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny enough, I imagine this NPC going though a thought process similar to this thread and realizing there is no easy way around someone else becoming a Martyr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:13:08-08:00","id":831206,"title":"","content":"Larceny and Medicine Excellencies and a ringer corpse harvested from one of the big cities accessible from Heaven via Yu-Shan gates -- that is, find someone with a very similar face and body shape as mine (or, similar face and body shape as my identity's), kidnap them, use Medicine to make them look as much like me as possible, and then fake my death in a way that allows me to murder them and make their corpse look like the result of my death. Possibly via fire.<br /> <br /> The trick is I need to keep the resplendent destiny active so people can remember that &quot;I&quot; exist at all -- it's no use faking my death if people forget I ever existed.<br /> <br /> What's my goal here? To what purpose am I faking my death and who am I trying to fool? If the answer is &quot;The Celestial Lions on behalf of a censor&quot; the answer above will not be sufficient. If the answer is just a general &quot;Everyone&quot; then you still need to define your terms, because, like, everyone including Jupiter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:15:41-08:00","id":831209,"title":"","content":"I think if you're looking for how to fake your death from the rest of the Fivescore Fellowship, the answer is &quot;Ahaha that's not a thing.&quot; They have procedures for finding my next incarnation; if I don't have one of those, they're going to expect shenanigans and investigate, and they <i>will</i> apply Occam's Razor to the situation and the simplest answer <i>will</i> be &quot;I'm not actually dead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:18:51-08:00","id":831213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831206#post831206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's my goal here? To what purpose am I faking my death and who am I trying to fool? If the answer is &quot;The Celestial Lions on behalf of a censor&quot; the answer above will not be sufficient. If the answer is just a general &quot;Everyone&quot; then you still need to define your terms, because, like, everyone including Jupiter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals and maybe a Solar or three (kind of doubtful on that last one, due to Investigation Charms). Basically people who knew that particular Resplendent Destiny. None of these people will know that the NPC is a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-16-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:29:52-08:00","id":831218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831206#post831206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larceny and Medicine Excellencies and a ringer corpse harvested from one of the big cities accessible from Heaven via Yu-Shan gates -- that is, find someone with a very similar face and body shape as mine (or, similar face and body shape as my identity's), kidnap them, use Medicine to make them look as much like me as possible, and then fake my death in a way that allows me to murder them and make their corpse look like the result of my death. Possibly via fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That springs to mind a question, can we use an elsewhere charm charm, while using the said body as a weapon via infernal monster style , to bring it back at the oportune moment back to creation to fake our death?? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:37:17-08:00","id":831226,"title":"","content":"I'm still blaming the theoretical Lion Lunar until proven otherwise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:43:06-08:00","id":831230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831226#post831226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still blaming the theoretical Lion Lunar until proven otherwise</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say it has nothing to do with the Ex3 game, but you wouldn't believe me anyways. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:00:35-08:00","id":831239,"title":"","content":"It's far more likely to be for Svante's campaign but PC Sidereal paranoia never truly goes away. No, not even when one of the pc's is a sidereal themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:06:28-08:00","id":831240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831239#post831239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's far more likely to be for Svante's campaign but PC Sidereal paranoia never truly goes away. No, not even when one of the pc's is a sidereal themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The question turns from &quot;Is this NPC a Sidereal?&quot; to &quot;Shit! What the fuck is this Sidereal doing here?!?&quot; *hides*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:14:05-08:00","id":831244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831218#post831218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That springs to mind a question, can we use an elsewhere charm charm, while using the said body as a weapon via infernal monster style , to bring it back at the oportune moment back to creation to fake our death?? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like Sidereal-appropriate levels of shenanigan, so I'd say sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:23:24-08:00","id":831249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831209#post831209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you're looking for how to fake your death from the rest of the Fivescore Fellowship, the answer is &quot;Ahaha that's not a thing.&quot; They have procedures for finding my next incarnation; if I don't have one of those, they're going to expect shenanigans and investigate, and they <i>will</i> apply Occam's Razor to the situation and the simplest answer <i>will</i> be &quot;I'm not actually dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe you could pretend to be your next incarnation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/957-wulfram","name":"Wulfram","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:28:38-08:00","id":831252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulfram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831249#post831249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe you could pretend to be your next incarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quicksilver Hand of Dreams SMA can help with this. If you use some the charms too much, even other Sidereals can forget about you.<br /> <br /> It's probably one of the many reasons why Elder Sidereals are so wary of Quicksilver practitioners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:30:50-08:00","id":831256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulfram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831249#post831249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe you could pretend to be your next incarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div>After I die, my next incarnation is an infant and has to grow into adolescence until the Sidereal Essence in its soul can flower into full bloom and turn her/him into a full Sidereal Exalted. 2e added some bit about how this doesn't apply to Sidereals who die unexpectedly, but that was not the case in 1e, didn't make a lot of sense (Given 5000 lifespans and high-danger jobs, far more Sidereals should die unexpectedly than not, so why does the setting treat raising new Sidereals from birth as the norm? The long wait between the death of one Sidereal and a replacement is considered a major problem for the Fivescore Fellowship, so wouldn't that make unexpected death the superior option if unexpected death eliminates it?), and should not be assumed to be in play for 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:33:51-08:00","id":831259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831256#post831256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After I die, my next incarnation is an infant and has to grow into adolescence until the Sidereal Essence in its soul can flower into full bloom and turn her/him into a full Sidereal Exalted. 2e added some bit about how this doesn't apply to Sidereals who die unexpectedly, but that was not the case in 1e, didn't make a lot of sense (Given 5000 lifespans and high-danger jobs, far more Sidereals should die unexpectedly than not, so why does the setting treat raising new Sidereals from birth as the norm? The long wait between the death of one Sidereal and a replacement is considered a major problem for the Fivescore Fellowship, so wouldn't that make unexpected death the superior option if unexpected death eliminates it?), and should not be assumed to be in play for 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this imply the assumption should be &quot;new Sidereal incarnation starts at birth&quot; or &quot;new Sidereal incarnation starts at adult&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:40:02-08:00","id":831264,"title":"","content":"The assumption is that Sidereal Exaltation start at birth; the Fivescore Fellowship uses vaguely-defined astrological prediction magic to track the birth down and then shape the infant's life until adolescence and the realization of the Exaltation. This can involve meddling in the child's life (if its birth circumstancces are discovered to be fortuitous) or kidnapping the infant and planting it in a wholly manufactured community (more common). Rarely, things can go wrong and Heaven can either fail to find the Exaltation or can lose track of the growing child, but usually things proceed within acceptable tolerance of just-as-planned.<br /> <br /> This makes faking your death as a Sidereal really hard!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:47:59-08:00","id":831270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831264#post831264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Fivescore Fellowship uses vaguely-defined astrological prediction magic</div> </div> </div> </div>75% of Cool Astrology things Sidereals do is Vaguely Defined. I just head canon it as &quot;Maidens send a memo saying when a new Sidereal is born. What the Five Score Fellowship does with this information is up to them. Every once in a while, a Maiden will not inform the Fellowship of a new incarnation, preferring to shape the child's destiny herself.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831264#post831264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes faking your death as a Sidereal really hard!</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume at least one Sidereal was stupid enough to try it.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:48:12-08:00","id":831271,"title":"","content":"Do you just need to be seen dying, or does your body need to be on display long-term?<br /> <br /> The opening charm of Ebon Shadow Style lets you credibly fake your own death in the former case. No disguise or illusion, just good old fashioned temporary heartrate stoppage.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, the question of whether you're trying to hide from the Sidereal Host is important here. I imagine things like this will be more plausible in 3E than 2E just because perfect competency and knowledge ruins so many good story ideas like this one, but even in 3E this is still going to be one of the highest challenge tiers for this type of con.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:51:40-08:00","id":831274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeptic Tank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831271#post831271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you just need to be seen dying, or does your body need to be on display long-term?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not hiding from the Sidereals, Celestial Lions, Yu-Shan, Auditors, Censors, or anyone else. Just some mortals. I suppose a Sidereal or two would show up to the funeral to make some smart comments about &quot;Bob&quot;. <br /> <br /> Ideally, dead long enough to be buried some where. If someone digs up the coffin and finds it empty, then someone stole the corpse!<br /> <br /> Though, I thought of a funny scene where the PCs disregard the NPCs wishes and attempts to cremate the body. Having the corpse suddenly wake up and protest the cremation sounds hysterical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-16-2016, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:34:05-08:00","id":831357,"title":"","content":"So, if you said it elsewhere I missed it\u2026 this Sidereal is an ally of the PCs, right? Because if he's their enemy, it won't matter if he bleeds out in front of them, they're more like than not to saw his head off and throw it into a furnace to &quot;make sure.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T17:39:06-08:00","id":831381,"title":"","content":"If you have to fake your death at all, one assumes you're dealing with people who can see through a Resplendent Destiny, because otherwise, why bother?<br /> <br /> So, Stephenls' concept of finding someone who looks a lot like you and kidnapping them has merit. Especially if you need a corpse, and can't get by on explosions/falling off a cliff/being swallowed by a Tyrant Lizard/whatever. HINT: always try to not leave a body if possible. Much fewer things can potentially go wrong.<br /> <br /> But if you DO need a body, and lack the time to find a body double, there's always Spirits! Get a shapechanging spirit, bind them, and have them assume your form, play dead for a while, and then Dematerialize and leave. Pretty straightforward, and even if your &quot;killers&quot; do saw off the head to make sure, at most, they'll uncover the spirit - you're out of there.<br /> <br /> If you don't even have time for that, just lie really still (Ebon Shadow Style is helpful here, as in many things), and once they start to bury/cremate you, Avoidance Kata out. It's not a perfect solution (these days, it seems to get harder and harder using Avoidance Kata after accomplishing anything else...), but it'll do in a pinch.<br /> <br /> All of that can be avoided if you simply use sorcery (at crudest, a Neomah - more sophisticated methods are better) to create an exact double of yourself, kill them cleanly, and then throw the body in an Elsewhere Egg. It won't decay, and if you ever need to die on short notice, just call the egg, drop the corpse, use the appropriate Someone Else's Destiny variant to give them any distinctive wounds/poisons/curses your would-be killers know to look for, and get out of there (Avoidance Kata optional, but preferred). It even works for escaping tedious social events with annoying co-workers (or any given Mouth Of Peace).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T17:47:10-08:00","id":831384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831381#post831381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have to fake your death at all, one assumes you're dealing with people who can see through a Resplendent Destiny, because otherwise, why bother?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's less the Sidereal faking their death and more the Resplendent Destiny the Sidereal is wearing. <br /> <br /> I really can't give that many details. The players are on this forum, though there is only a slim chance this character would fake their death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T18:36:03-08:00","id":831407,"title":"","content":"When a RD expires normally, what happens? IIRC, it basically works like Arcane Fate, and the people who knew the destiny still kinda-sorta remember that she existed in that they remember that <i>someone</i> was responsible for the things she did, but get fuzzier and fuzzier on the details and think about her less and less. So if the Sidereal decided to martyr her RD for a cause, for those who couldn't see through it, there probably wouldn't be much practical difference between a dramatic fake death and a simple one. The RD is last seen charging the battlements or whatever, doesn't come back, his former friends vow to avenge him (maybe egged on by a <i>different</i> RD who says he <i>totally </i>saw the body), the revolution ignites, the Sidereal lets the first RD lapse, and by the time the dust settles they're putting up a statue to that heroic, nameless revolutionary who everyone remembers started the revolution, but no one quite agrees how tall to make the statue. Most importantly, they also agree he's not around anymore. The symbol survives, but the identity dies, which is all you really needed.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a Gavroche-as-Chosen-of-Battles idea I once had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-16-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:35:43-08:00","id":831820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831407#post831407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a RD expires normally, what happens? IIRC, it basically works like Arcane Fate, and the people who knew the destiny still kinda-sorta remember that she existed in that they remember that <i>someone</i> was responsible for the things she did, but get fuzzier and fuzzier on the details and think about her less and less. So if the Sidereal decided to martyr her RD for a cause, for those who couldn't see through it, there probably wouldn't be much practical difference between a dramatic fake death and a simple one. The RD is last seen charging the battlements or whatever, doesn't come back, his former friends vow to avenge him (maybe egged on by a <i>different</i> RD who says he <i>totally </i>saw the body), the revolution ignites, the Sidereal lets the first RD lapse, and by the time the dust settles they're putting up a statue to that heroic, nameless revolutionary who everyone remembers started the revolution, but no one quite agrees how tall to make the statue. Most importantly, they also agree he's not around anymore. The symbol survives, but the identity dies, which is all you really needed.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a Gavroche-as-Chosen-of-Battles idea I once had.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've got a real, relatively recent example coming in mind now you're describing how this could work: Tiananmen Square's Tank Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:38:57-08:00","id":831824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831820#post831820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've got a real, relatively recent example coming in mind now you're describing how this could work: Tiananmen Square's Tank Man.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If this is RD ending as normal, then I have no need for crazy schemes to make the &quot;RD as a Martyr&quot; idea work.<br /> <br /> My next question is about Arcane Fate. Is Arcane Fate more &quot;Who the fuck was that guy?&quot; or &quot;What guy?&quot; <br /> <br /> And does Arcane Fate apply different to a Sidereal without RD and a Resplendent Destiny that has ended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:46:27-08:00","id":831830,"title":"","content":"I've always answered your first question with &quot;Whatever is needed for my story.&quot; The more involved a person is though, the more I suspect it becomes the former answer and not the latter answer.<br /> <br /> No idea about it's interaction with RD though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:21:34-08:00","id":831852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831264#post831264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The assumption is that Sidereal Exaltation starts at birth</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to the next thread, Dramatic Birth Scene - how would a Sidereal fake being a newborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:27:28-08:00","id":831857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831852#post831852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking forward to the next thread, Dramatic Birth Scene - how would a Sidereal fake being a newborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that as &quot;how would a Sidereal fake being a neverborn&quot;<br /> <br /> Now THERE'S a charm I'd get some fun out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:32:07-08:00","id":831863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831852#post831852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking forward to the next thread, Dramatic Birth Scene - how would a Sidereal fake being a newborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I knew how to draw because know I have a image of Adult sized Kejak shoved in a playpen with a pacifier and a bow on his head. He has the stereotypical Stern Kejak expression. Jupiter or Ayesha is standing by the play pen saying &quot;Jack gets grouchy when he doesn't get his nap.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:40:08-08:00","id":831868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831863#post831863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I knew how to draw because know I have a image of Adult sized Kejak shoved in a playpen with a pacifier and a bow on his head. He has the stereotypical Stern Kejak expression. Jupiter or Ayesha is standing by the play pen saying &quot;Jack gets grouchy when he doesn't get his nap.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is EXACTLY like that.<br /> <br /> That scene at the end of RotSE gets real funny really fast, if the book hadn't ended when it did. Green Lady is, like, five different babies you never see in the same place at once. Black Ice Shadow is writing sad poetry with alphabet blocks. Ahn Aru was a stillbirth whose canon status is uncertain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:16:32-08:00","id":831957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831863#post831863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish I knew how to draw because know I have a image of Adult sized Kejak shoved in a playpen with a pacifier and a bow on his head. He has the stereotypical Stern Kejak expression. Jupiter or Ayesha is standing by the play pen saying &quot;Jack gets grouchy when he doesn't get his nap.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't draw, but I can write. I threw this together real quick at lunch:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cAny Resplendent Destiny?\u201d Ayesha asked skeptically.<br /> <br /> \u201cAny.\u201d Chejop knew Ayesha would never let such a boast go unchallenged. \u201cI\u2019ve been alive for five Millennia. There is not much I haven\u2019t done. \u201c<br /> <br /> Ayesha scowled, tapping her pen against her notepad. \u201cI can\u2019t imagine you mopping floors.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll be surprised what people say in front of janitors. It\u2019s like you don\u2019t even exist.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFur Trader?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you have to butcher a mink, avoid the nicking the scent glands. Not only does it ruin the fur your hands will reek for at least a week.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSchool Teacher?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI find children react rather well to a consistent and firm hand.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ayesha grinned. \u201cI know one Identity you have never taken.\u201d<br /> <br /> When Ayesha began to pack up her notebook, Chejop said, \u201cDon\u2019t leave me in suspense. What is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo\u2026 There is no point in mentioning it.\u201d Ayesha stood from her chair and turned to leave his office. \u201cA man of your statue will never don such a destiny.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAyesha, I have been the secretary of the Mouth of Peace for twelve consecutive destinies. I have no problem taking on the humblest of roles.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, you have had a lot of practice being the bumbling fool.\u201d She set her bag down on his desk. \u201cWould you care for a wager?\u201d<br /> <br /> Chejop steepled his fingers. Ayesha was always a gambler. It was what lead her down this foolhardy path to begin with. \u201cWhat did you have in mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA favor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Chejop crossed his arms. \u201cYou are not getting an open ended favor. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd if I tell you what I want, you\u2019ll take the information and kick me out of your office.\u201d<br /> <br /> Chejop suppressed a smile. Ayesha was always the brightest of his students. A shame she was overly influenced by Tammiz's memories. Chejop sighed. \u201cYou are not getting an open ended favor. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess we are done here.\u201d Ayesha picked up her bag and headed towards the door. \u201cSame time next week?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWait. At least tell me what destiny you were thinking of.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ayesha paused at the door and looks back. \u201cOnly if you agree to the wager.\u201d<br /> <br /> Chejop stroked his chin and considered the situation. The Destiny Ayesha had in mind must be humiliating. Might be best to let her go. There were other ways to find out what the Gold Faction Leader was planning. Yet was there really a Resplendent Destiny he, Chejop Kejak, couldn\u2019t protray? Probably not, but he didn\u2019t need to prove it to this woman. Yes, it would be best to let Ayesha go.<br /> <br /> Instead he found himself saying, \u201cWhen I don this destiny there will be no gods, exalts, or anyone immune to Arcane Fate within 100 miles. No recording devices either.\u201d He didn\u2019t know why he lets Ayesha gloat him into these situations.<br /> <br /> Ayesha deflated at this condition, but agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou will be with me the entire time.\u201d If there was danger, then she will encounter it with him.<br /> <br /> Ayesha smiled. \u201cThat would be best I think.\u201d<br /> <br /> What was this destiny? Chejop added a few other precautionary conditions and the wager was set.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have a single Wyld Hunt patrolling the Coast of the White Sea. I want them assigned elsewhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> Chejop rustled though his drawers for Prayer Stripes and Ink. Ayesha\u2019s request seemed very transparent. She must have a circle of Solars in that area. He would think about that later. \u201cWhat is the Destiny?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cAwww\u2026.\u201d An older woman peered down at Chejop with a goofy smile on her face. \u201cWhat an adorable baby! Looks just like a grumpy old man! Is it a boy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d Ayesha replied with a saccharine smile. She grabed the woman\u2019s hand before she could pat Chejop\u2019s head. \u201cI wouldn\u2019t. Jack gets grouchy when he doesn\u2019t get his nap.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Maidens bless you, Ayesha.</i> Chejop thought as Ayesha gets lectures about the benefits of giving babies whiskey for colic. Bad enough he was crammed into this crib, but if someone actually patted him on his head\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cMaidens,\u201d Ayesha muttered, after the woman finally leaves. \u201cI thought dealing with the kid would be the worst part of parenting. \u201d<br /> <br /> Chejop fidgeted with the pacifier in his mouth and smiled. There wasn\u2019t a Resplendent Destiny he couldn\u2019t pull off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Fixed the spelling the name of Ayesha's previous incarnation 02-17-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T18:16:20-08:00","id":832221,"title":"","content":"&quot;\u2026Tazmin?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T18:35:06-08:00","id":832227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=832221#post832221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;\u2026Tazmin?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whatever the fuck that guys name is. The one that Kejak choked to death. I did this at work in less than a hour, god damn it! You could at least give me the correct spelling if you are going to point out my errors! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:04:27-08:00","id":832240,"title":"","content":"The name is Tammiz Ushun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:14:20-08:00","id":832248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=832240#post832240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name is Tammiz Ushun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T05:18:35-08:00","id":835683,"title":"","content":"Was thinking about this discussion while running this morning. Turns out you don't really need a body to fake your own death. Instead, what you do is 'die' in such a way that your body could likely never be found. Then you show up to your followers one night disguised as your own ghost. Pretending to be a ghost should be much easier than leaving a convincing body behind and you have much more control over what actually happens by being there.<br /> <br /> Also, has anybody asked Jen yet if they could maybe pretty please, draw Baby Kejak? Seems like exactly the right person to do that kind for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T06:45:32-08:00","id":835717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=835683#post835683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was thinking about this discussion while running this morning. Turns out you don't really need a body to fake your own death. Instead, what you do is 'die' in such a way that your body could likely never be found.</div> </div> </div> </div>This still doesn't fool the Fivescore Fellowship, for the record. Or a team of genre-savvy players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=835683#post835683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you show up to your followers one night disguised as your own ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prepare for them trying to summon you, soulforge you, social-fu you into using your ghostly powers to benefit them, or send you to Lethe, if you're playing 2e. Or your enemies deciding they didn't kill you hard enough, if word gets to them of your spookiness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=835683#post835683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretending to be a ghost should be much easier than leaving a convincing body behind and you have much more control over what actually happens by being there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying, count on player characters to be player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:04:41-08:00","id":835734,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wrote that from the perspective of the Sid in question being a Player trying to convince a largely mortal group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:11:03-08:00","id":835742,"title":"","content":"The Sid's a player character, not an NPC? Where was that said?<br /> <br /> EDIT: OP says on the first page that the guy's an NPC. Now I suppose the question becomes, &quot;Are the mortals he's supposed to be fooling, in fact, PCs?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:03:20-08:00","id":835809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=831206#post831206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larceny and Medicine Excellencies and a ringer corpse harvested from one of the big cities accessible from Heaven via Yu-Shan gates -- that is, find someone with a very similar face and body shape as mine (or, similar face and body shape as my identity's), kidnap them, use Medicine to make them look as much like me as possible, and then fake my death in a way that allows me to murder them and make their corpse look like the result of my death. Possibly via fire.<br /> <br /> The trick is I need to keep the resplendent destiny active so people can remember that &quot;I&quot; exist at all -- it's no use faking my death if people forget I ever existed.<br /> <br /> What's my goal here? To what purpose am I faking my death and who am I trying to fool? If the answer is &quot;The Celestial Lions on behalf of a censor&quot; the answer above will not be sufficient. If the answer is just a general &quot;Everyone&quot; then you still need to define your terms, because, like, everyone including Jupiter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm late to the party, but..... is anyone else alarmed that this is written in first person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:18:55-08:00","id":835860,"title":"","content":"Okay, this (obviously) draws from 2E. But, as was said in the OP, the Siddie is trying to fake the death of a <u>Resplendent Destiny</u>. This is much easier than faking the death of an actual Sidereal. The fact that he is trying to fake the death of a Resplendent Destiny clearly implies he isn't trying to fool other Sidereals, because Siddies can automatically see through RDs. Likewise, probably not trying to fool heaven...because again, it's a Resplendent Destiny.<br /> <br /> So, what needs to happen in order to functionally fool people into thinking a Resplendent Destiny is dead? Well, you need a body that looks just like your Resplendent Destiny, and cannot be proven to be otherwise. Even if someone was aware you were a supernatural being, in death the Exaltation departs the body so a corpse wouldn't register on supernatural senses anyway. The absolute simplest way to do this would be to take someone you don't mind being dead and capture them. You render them unconscious, then use the spell Disguise of the New Face on them. This spell is incredibly convenient in that it is persistent until the Sorcerer dismisses it. Mundane attempts to pierce the disguise automatically fail, and charms that might be able to pierce it are subject to a roll-off against your spellcasting chops.<br /> <br /> So, in short, you have the ability to perfectly change someone to look just like your RD, and unless they break out some powerful Investigation charms and roll better than you do, it's going to fool everyone. This works even better if the Siddie in question used this spell in the first place to disguise themselves as their Resplendent Destiny (remember, Siddies get huge bonuses to disguising themselves), and don't <i>actually</i> look like that. It helps that DotNF also allows you to 'plug in' mannerisms that it supernaturally helps you maintain to further augment your disguise.<br /> <br /> So, here's the plan: You simply ensure that their 'death' occurs some distance away from the people you are trying to fool so that you can either simply kill the person you transformed into looking like you, or you can take the 'dive' yourself, make sure you land somewhere out of their line of sight, and swap places with the corpse. Heck, you could even handle the kill yourself by having another RD + Disguise that you use to actually make the kill. Then, some time after the funeral and once the body double is buried, you release that Resplendent Destiny, and let all memory of 'you' fade away into your Arcane Fate.<br /> <br /> And, if you are worried about them looking into it further, you don a new RD with a new face and abuse Walking Outside Fate, Subordinate Inspiration Method, Blinding the Boar, and Impose Motivation to very, VERY soundly get part of the group adamant that the group needs to let it go and carry on without the Siddie's fake identity. Use Presence in Absence Technique to support the social abilities of that person...Force Decision (to force the others to come down on the side of said decision you want). If necessary, use Thought Swiping Distraction to distract the investigator from looking into the 'true identity' of the corpse, possibly while disguised as a hobo and running Underling Invisibility Practice to make yourself unnoticeable to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T12:13:49-08:00","id":835920,"title":"","content":"Use shenanigans to learn the spirit charms of Mist the Eternal Revolutionary then get 5 in charisma and 5 in perform with a specialty in overblown speeched. Take a lethal hit then monologue until the person you're fighting gets bored and leaves and you are left unobserved, thus allowing you to use Mist's Disney-Villain Death Avoidance Prana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T12:22:55-08:00","id":835927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/831132-dramatic-death-scene-how-would-a-sidereal-fake-their-own-death?p=835860#post835860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this (obviously) draws from 2E. But, as was said in the OP, the Siddie is trying to fake the death of a <u>Resplendent Destiny</u>. This is much easier than faking the death of an actual Sidereal. The fact that he is trying to fake the death of a Resplendent Destiny clearly implies he isn't trying to fool other Sidereals, because Siddies can automatically see through RDs. Likewise, probably not trying to fool heaven...because again, it's a Resplendent Destiny.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm trying to create a Martyr for a Social Movement without having to actually kill someone from that movement. Basically, have the Resplendent Destiny be killed publicly. Allow the Resplendent Destiny continue, so people remember the Martyr. When the Social Movement grows beyond that Martyr, end the Destiny. People will forget who the Martyr was, but the social movement should survive (The original Sidereal will still be around to help things along).<br /> <br /> Heck there may be debates on who the Martyr was! Sort of like how most people think Jesus is a blue eyed white man who died on the cross, while others maintain Jesus never existed.<br /> <br /> To be honest, the idea no longer fits in my game, so it is all theoretical now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-23-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}